10. MS. MUNAZA HASSAN, Chairperson Standing Committee on Climate Change andEnvironmental Coordination, to present the Periodical Report of the Committee for the period 1't July,2024 to 31't December, 2024, as required by rule 234-4 of the Rules of Procedure and Conduct ofBusiness in the National Assembly, 2007.11. RAI HASSAN NAWAZ KHAN, Chairman Standing Committee on Railways, to present thePeriod ical Report of the Com m ittee for the period lst July, 2024 to 31st Decem be r, 2024, as req uiredby rule 234-4 ofthe Rules of Procedure and Conduct of Business in the National Assembly, 2007.
L2. DR. MAHESH KUMAR MALANI, Chairman Standing Committee on National Health Services,Regulations and Coordination, to present the Periodical Report of the Committee for the periodlst July, 2024 to 31st December, 2024, as required by rule 234-4 of the Rules of Procedure andConduct of Business in the National Assembly, 2007.
13. SYED HAFEEZUDDIN, Chairman Standing Committee on lndustries and Production, to presentthe Periodical Report of the Committee for the period 7'r )uly, 2024 to 31't December, 2024, asrequired by rule 234-4 of the Rules of Procedure and Conduct of Business in the National Assembly,2007.
14. MR. AZIM UDDIN ZAHID, Chairman Standing Committee on Federal Education, ProfessionalTraining, National Heritage and Culture, to present the Periodical Report of the Committee for theperiod 1't July, 2024 to 31st December, 2024, as required by rule 234-A of the Rules of Procedure andConduct of Business in the NationalAssembly, 2007.
15. MR. MUHAMMAD IDREES, Chairman Standing Committee on Energy (Power Division), topresent the Periodical Report of the Committee for the period \'t July,2024 to 31st December, 2024,as required by rule 234-4 ofthe Rules of Procedure and Conduct of Business in the NationalAssembly,2007 .MOTION OF THANKS
L6. Further discussion on the following motion moved by DR. TARIQ FAZAL CHAUDHARY,Minister for Parliamentary Affairs on 12th March, 2025:-
"This House expresses its deep gratitude to the President of the lslamic Republic of Pakistanfor his address to both Houses assembled together on 10th March, 2025."
MATTERS OTHER THAN POINTS OF ORDER
L7.
Raising matters under Rule 18 which are not Points of Order.CALLING ATTENTION NOTICE
18. MS. ATIYA KAMRAN MR. MUHAMMAD USMAN BADINI to invite attention ofthe Minister for Religious Affairs and lnterfaith Harmony to a matter of urgent public importanceregarding failure to secure private Hajj quota from Saudi Arabia for the Hajj in 2O25, causing graveconcern amongst the public.
TAHIR HUSSAINSecretary General
lslamabad, the9th April. 2025

